From c7e4c74ebf1a819cfccf86dd8f8c24d37b9a2171 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Apr 2026 10:55:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rebrand(2026): retint Artist Hub to BFTA palette + green-2
 BFTA bug
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bring the Svelte Artist Hub (artist-hub/) into the 2026 brand system. Hub
stays a dark UI (right call for nostr feeds + zap activity threads at
night) but every accent reads BFTA now.

Logo:
- artist-hub/static/bfta-logo.png is now a copy of the green-2 BFTA bug
  (lime field, black BTA, orange Arts script). Both AppHeader.svelte and
  routes/+page.svelte already point at /bfta-logo.png so no component
  edits were needed — same path, new asset.

Color tokens (artist-hub/src/app.css):
- --accent     #f6c453 (warm gold)  -> #b3ff48 (BFTA lime)
- --accent-2   #8b5cf6 (purple)     -> #ff4f14 (BFTA orange)
- --text       white                -> cream-tinted (FFFAF0 @ 94%)
- Body radial-gradient washes repainted from purple/gold/blue to
  lime/orange/cream so the page background mirrors the SiteBackground
  treatment on bitcoinforthearts.org.
- .btn.primary repainted with the lime tint (translucent overlay, same
  shape, so existing hover/disabled states are unaffected).

Inline rgba sweep across every .svelte/.ts/.css file in artist-hub/src:
- rgba(246, 196, 83, *)  -> rgba(179, 255, 72, *)   gold -> lime
- rgba(139, 92, 246, *)  -> rgba(255, 79, 20, *)    purple -> orange
- #f6c453 -> #b3ff48
- #8b5cf6 -> #ff4f14   (also catches the QR code dark color in
                       NpubShareModal.svelte so generated QR codes are
                       drawn in BFTA orange instead of purple.)

Affects ~26 files across components and routes — entirely color-token
changes, no structural / layout changes. Both 'npm run build' inside
artist-hub/ and the root Next.js prebuild (which packages the hub for
deploy) pass clean.

Co-authored-by: Dion Wilson <wilson.dion@proton.me>
